crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_computed_tags.sky:2:29: error: `A + Aᵀ` is not known to be Symmetric
  |
2 | S: Symmetric Matrix[2, 2] = A + Aᵀ
  |                             ^^^^^^ this is Matrix[2,2] [1]
  |    ---------------------- expected because of this annotation
  = note: the checker only knows a matrix property if it can prove it: from a declaration, or an operation that preserves it
  = help: `+`, `-`, scaling, negation, `ᵀ` and `⁻¹` of Symmetric matrices are Symmetric; for another matrix, pass it to a function whose parameter is declared Symmetric, which checks it when the function is called

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_computed_tags.sky:4:36: error: `P + P` is not known to be PositiveDefinite
  |
4 | Q: PositiveDefinite Matrix[2, 2] = P + P
  |                                    ^^^^^ this is Matrix[2,2] {Symmetric} [1]
  |    ----------------------------- expected because of this annotation
  = note: the checker only knows a matrix property if it can prove it: from a declaration, or an operation that preserves it
  = help: only `ᵀ` and `⁻¹` keep PositiveDefinite; for a matrix you know is positive definite, pass it to a function whose parameter is declared PositiveDefinite: its symmetry is checked when the function is called, and its positivity by the Cholesky solve that relies on it

